<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernard Coard</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1944">1944</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernard Coard is a Grenadian politician who was deputy prime minister in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurice-bishop">Maurice Bishop</a>'s People's Revolutionary Government. In October 1983 his faction in the New Jewel Movement placed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> under house arrest, and Bishop and several ministers were shot on 19 October, events that led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> invasion. Coard was convicted over the killings, spent many years in prison and was released in 2009.</p></div>
